{
  "version": 1,
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Lab 3 — CampusWeather Connector & RequestWeather"
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "kind": 1,
      "language": "markdown",
      "value": "# Lab 3 — `CampusWeather` Connector & `RequestWeather` Action\n\nA **Connector** bridges MQTT topics to an external system — here, the free [Open-Meteo HTTPS API](https://open-meteo.com/) (no API key needed).\n\n### How the two pieces work together\n1. **`CampusWeather` (REST Connector):** Listens on `campus/weather/fetch`. Whenever a message arrives on that topic, it appends the message payload (the query string) to `https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast` and publishes the HTTP JSON response to `campus/weather/raw`.\n2. **`RequestWeather` (Action):** Runs every 60 seconds (`ON EVERY 60 SECONDS DO`) **and** whenever you publish anything to `campus/weather/request` (`ON TOPIC \"campus/weather/request\" DO`). It reads `WEATHER_LAT` and `WEATHER_LON` from the environment variables you set in `00-setup` and publishes the query string to `campus/weather/fetch`.\n\n### Cell 1: Deploy the `CampusWeather` Connector\nClick **▷** on the cell below:"
    },
    {
      "kind": 2,
      "language": "lot",
      "value": "DEFINE CONNECTOR CampusWeather WITH TYPE REST\n    ADD REST_CONFIG\n        WITH BASE_URL \"https://api.open-meteo.com\"\n        WITH TIMEOUT 10\n        WITH VERIFY_SSL TRUE\n    ADD EVENT FetchCurrent\n        WITH SOURCE_TOPIC \"campus/weather/fetch\"\n        WITH DESTINATION_TOPIC \"campus/weather/raw\"\n        WITH METHOD \"GET\"\n        WITH ENDPOINT \"/v1/forecast\"\n        WITH QUERY_PARAMS_FROM_PAYLOAD TRUE\n"
    },
    {
      "kind": 1,
      "language": "markdown",
      "value": "### Cell 2: Deploy the `RequestWeather` Action\nClick **▷** on the cell below (or click **Deploy All** at the top right of the notebook):"
    },
    {
      "kind": 2,
      "language": "lot",
      "value": "DEFINE ACTION RequestWeather\nON EVERY 60 SECONDS DO\n    SET \"lat\" WITH (GET ENV \"WEATHER_LAT\")\n    SET \"lon\" WITH (GET ENV \"WEATHER_LON\")\n    PUBLISH TOPIC \"campus/weather/fetch\" WITH \"?latitude=\" + {lat} + \"&longitude=\" + {lon} + \"&current=temperature_2m,wind_speed_10m,weather_code\"\nON TOPIC \"campus/weather/request\" DO\n    SET \"lat\" WITH (GET ENV \"WEATHER_LAT\")\n    SET \"lon\" WITH (GET ENV \"WEATHER_LON\")\n    PUBLISH TOPIC \"campus/weather/fetch\" WITH \"?latitude=\" + {lat} + \"&longitude=\" + {lon} + \"&current=temperature_2m,wind_speed_10m,weather_code\"\n"
    },
    {
      "kind": 1,
      "language": "markdown",
      "value": "### Trigger an immediate weather fetch\n\nYou don't have to wait 60 seconds for the timer:\n1. Open **Data Viewer → Publish**.\n2. Publish payload `poll` to topic **`campus/weather/request`**.\n3. Check **`campus/weather/raw`** (the live Open-Meteo response) and **`campus/weather/reading`** (automatically processed by your Lab 2 Action!).\n\n**Next up:** Open **`04-heat-alert-history-email.lotnb`** to add heat alerts, CSV logging, and email notifications."
    }
  ]
}
